    "problemStatement": "For a (000-indexed) binary string SSS of length NNN, define f(S)=f(S) = f(S)= the number of pairs (i,j)(i, j) (i,j) such that 0≤i&lt;j&lt;N0 \\leq i \\lt j \\lt N0≤i&lt;j&lt;N and Si=0,Sj=1S_i = 0, S_j = 1Si​=0,Sj​=1.\n\nGiven a binary string SSS of size NNN, you can perform the following operation **exactly once**:\n\n\nChoose an integer KKK such that 1&lt;K≤N1 \\lt K \\le N1&lt;K≤N and N mod K=0N \\bmod K = 0NmodK=0, and divide the string into continuous substrings of size KKK, i.e. you will have a list of NK\\frac{N}{K}KN​ substrings S[0,K−1],S[K,2⋅K−1],…,S[N−K,N−1]S[0, K-1], S[K, 2 \\cdot K-1], \\ldots, S[N - K, N-1]S[0,K−1],S[K,2⋅K−1],…,S[N−K,N−1].\n\nHere, S[L,R]S[L, R]S[L,R] denotes the string formed by concatenating the characters SL,SL+1,SL+2,…,SRS_L, S_{L + 1}, S_{L + 2}, \\ldots, S_RSL​,SL+1​,SL+2​,…,SR​ in this order.\n\n\nRearrange the list of NK\\frac{N}{K}KN​ substrings in some order, and concatenate the substrings to form the new string SSS.\nFind the **maximum** possible value of f(S)f(S)f(S) after this operation has been performed.\n\nYou will be given the string SSS in encoded format.\n\nWe will provide you with an array AAA of size M=⌈N30⌉M = \\left\\lceil \\frac{N}{30} \\right\\rceilM=⌈30N​⌉. The original character SiS_iSi​ can be obtained as\n\nf(A[&nbsp;&nbsp;⌊i30⌋&nbsp;&nbsp;],i mod 30)f\\left(A\\left[\\ \\ \\left\\lfloor \\frac{i}{30} \\right\\rfloor\\ \\ \\right], i \\bmod 30\\right)f(A[&nbsp;&nbsp;⌊30i​⌋&nbsp;&nbsp;],imod30)where f(x,y)f(x, y)f(x,y) represents the yyy-th bit of xxx, and ⌊x⌋\\left\\lfloor x \\right\\rfloor⌊x⌋ is the largest integer that doesn't exceed xxx.\n\nConsider array AAA and the string SSS to be 000-indexed.\n\nSee the samples below for more clarity on the input format.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line contains two integers NNN and MMM — the length of string SSS, and the length of the encoded array AAA, respectively.\nThe second line contains MMM space-separated integers A0,A1,…,AM−1A_0, A_1, \\ldots, A_{M-1}A0​,A1​,…,AM−1​ — the encoded array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the maximum value of f(S)f(S)f(S) after one operation.",
